<title>AUSTRALIA: Western Australia wants labour reform bill passed.</title>
<headline>Western Australia wants labour reform bill passed.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Western Australian state government is determined to get its new industrial relations bill through Parliament despite threats of a national blockade and a long industrial campaign, Labour Relations Minister Graham Kierath said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We did buckle last time (when similar legislation was introduced, in 1996),&quot; the minister in the conservative coalition government told Reuters.</p>
</text>
